king) keeps aeon on and you act at a crawl." }, mindlock = { affs = { "deadening", "mindclamp", "scrambledbrains" }, desc = "Telepathy (Monk). Deadening makes the lock easier; scrambledbrains stops you breaking it." }, instakill = { affs = { "voyria", "heartseed", "latched", "bruisedribs", "enlightenment" }, desc = "Afflictions that are, or set up, a kill." }, }
-- Derived indexes ---------------------------------------------------------- AFF.aliases = {} -- other spellings -> GMCP name AFF.by_cmd = {} -- "eat kelp" -> { affs it can cure } (alphabetical, NOT priority order) AFF.by_item = {} -- "kelp" / "aurum" -> same list (both twins) AFF.blockers = {} -- "eat" -> { "anorexia" }, "focus" -> { "impatience" }, ... AFF.hinderers = {} AFF.focusable = {} for name, a in pairs(AFF.affs) do a.name = name a.cmds = a.cmds or {} for _, al in ipairs(a.aliases or {}) do AFF.aliases[al] = name end for _, c in ipairs(a.cmds) do AFF.by_cmd[c] = AFF.by_cmd[c] or {} table.insert(AFF.by_cmd[c], name) end for _, c in ipairs(a.cures) do for _, it in ipairs({ c.item, c.alt }) do AFF.by_item[it] = AFF.by_item[it] or {} table.insert(AFF.by_item[it], name) end end for _, b in ipairs(a.blocks or {}) do AFF.blockers[b] = AFF.blockers[b] or {} table.insert(AFF.blockers[b], name) end for _, b in ipairs(a.hinders or {}) do AFF.hinderers[b] = AFF.hinderers[b] or {} table.insert(AFF.hinderers[b], name) end if a.focus then AFF.focusable[name] = true end end for _, t in pairs({ AFF.by_cmd, AFF.by_item, AFF.blockers, AFF.hinderers }) do for _, list in pairs(t) do table.sort(list) end end
-- Normalise any spelling ("Broken Left Arm", "paralysed") to the GMCP name. function AFF.canon(name) if not name then return nil end local n = tostring(name):lower():gsub("[%s_%-']", "") return AFF.aliases[n] or n end
function AFF.get(name) return AFF.affs[AFF.canon(name)] end
-- First fallback command for an affliction, or nil when it has none. function AFF.cure_cmd(name) local a = AFF.get(name) return a and a.cmds[1] end
-- Is a cure channel blocked given a set of current afflictions ({ name = true })? function AFF.blocked(channel, affs) for _, n in ipairs(AFF.blockers[channel] or {}) do if affs[n] then return n end end return nil end
achaea_affs = AFF return AFF

-- AR data: everything offense needs to know about how an ENEMY cures. -- Kept separate from the curing package's data on purpose, so AR works on -- its own and either package can change its tables freely. -- -- Names are normalised (lowercase, no spaces/underscores/dashes).
ar = ar or {} ar.data = ar.data or {} local D = ar.data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- -- Venoms -> the affliction they give. -- "crippledarm"/"crippledleg" resolve to whichever side isn't broken yet. -- delphinium strips insomnia first, then puts them to sleep (see enemy.venom). D.venoms = { curare = "paralysis", kalmia = "asthma", gecko = "slickness", slike = "anorexia", xentio = "clumsiness", prefarar = "sensitivity", aconite = "stupidity", euphorbia = "nausea", darkshade = "darkshade", vernalius = "weariness", epteth = "crippledarm", epseth = "crippledleg", digitalis = "shyness", monkshood = "disloyalty", eurypteria = "recklessness", larkspur = "dizziness", oleander = "blindness", colocasia = { "blindness", "deafness" }, delphinium = "asleep", vardrax = "addiction", notechis = "haemophilia", voyria = "voyria", scytherus = "scytherus", selarnia = "selarnia", nechamandra = "shivering", } D.aff_to_venom = {} for v, a in pairs(D.venoms) do if type(a) == "string" then D.aff_to_venom[a] = v end end D.aff_to_venom.deafness = "colocasia" D.aff_to_venom.brokenleftarm, D.aff_to_venom.brokenrightarm = "epteth", "epteth" D.aff_to_venom.brokenleftleg, D.aff_to_venom.brokenrightleg = "epseth", "epseth"
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- -- What each curative cures, in the order an enemy usually cures them -- (roughly serverside default priority). When we see them eat kelp we -- remove the first of these they have. D.herb_cures = { bloodroot = { "paralysis", "slickness" }, kelp = { "asthma", "clumsiness", "sensitivity", "weariness", "hypochondria", "healthleech", "parasite" }, ginseng = { "haemophilia", "darkshade", "nausea", "addiction", "lethargy", "scytherus", "flushings" }, goldenseal = { "impatience", "stupidity", "dizziness", "epilepsy", "shyness", "dissonance", "depression", "shadowmadness" }, lobelia = { "recklessness", "agoraphobia", "masochism", "claustrophobia", "vertigo", "loneliness", "spiritburn", "tenderskin" }, ash = { "confusion", "hallucinations", "dementia", "paranoia", "hypersomnia" }, bellwort = { "pacifism", "peace", "generosity", "justice", "inlove", "retribution", "timeloop" }, pear = { "drowning", "pressure" }, ginger = { "temperedcholeric", "temperedmelancholic", "temperedphlegmatic", "temperedsanguine" }, }
-- Words in "X eats ..." -> herb key (minerals from transmute too). D.herb_words = { bloodroot = "bloodroot", magnesium = "bloodroot", kelp = "kelp", aurum = "kelp", ginseng = "ginseng", ferrum = "ginseng", goldenseal = "goldenseal", plumbum = "goldenseal", lobelia = "lobelia", argentum = "lobelia", ash = "ash", stannum = "ash", bellwort = "bellwort", cuprum = "bellwort", pear = "pear", calcite = "pear", ginger = "ginger", antimony = "ginger", }
-- Salve location (as seen in "rubs it on his <loc>") -> what it may cure. D.salve_cures = { legs = { "brokenleftleg", "brokenrightleg", "mangledleftleg", "mangledrightleg", "damagedleftleg", "damagedrightleg" }, arms = { "brokenleftarm", "brokenrightarm", "mangledleftarm", "mangledrightarm", "damagedleftarm", "damagedrightarm" }, head = { "mangledhead", "damagedhead", "crushedthroat", "stuttering", "blindness", "deafness", "indifference", "blurryvision" }, torso = { "serioustrauma", "mildtrauma", "heatspear", "collapsedlung", "crackedribs", "damagedtorso" }, body = { "anorexia", "ablaze", "selarnia", "itching", "gorged", "effused", "shivering", "frozen" }, } D.salve_cures.skin = D.salve_cures.body D.salve_cures.chest = D.salve_cures.torso D.salve_cures.gut = D.salve_cures.torso
-- valerian and elm look the same from outside ("a long drag off his pipe") D.smoke_cures = { "aeon", "slickness", "disloyalty", "deadening", "hellsight", "manaleech", "disfigurement", "dazed" }
-- FOCUS cures one of these (mental afflictions). -- (the wiki's affliction table; stupidity is not on it) D.focus_cures = { "anorexia", "recklessness", "dizziness", "confusion", "epilepsy", "shyness", "agoraphobia", "claustrophobia", "loneliness", "hallucinations", "dementia", "inlove", } D.focusable = {} for _, a in ipairs(D.focus_cures) do D.focusable[a] = true end
-- What blocks each way of curing. D.blocks = { eat = { "anorexia" }, smoke = { "asthma" }, apply = { "slickness", "bloodfire" }, focus = { "impatience", "sandfever" }, tree = { "paralysis", "icefisted" }, }
-- How long each enemy curative balance takes (seconds). Used to tell when -- they can cure again; adjust with "ar ebal <kind> <seconds>". AW's times, -- the same SS uses for you (ss.bal_timeouts). Restoration takes 4s, but the -- apply line doesn't say which salve, so apply uses the 1s of the others. D.enemy_bal = { eat = 1.5, apply = 1.0, smoke = 1.5, focus = 2.5, tree = 14.0 }
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- -- Enemy defences AR tracks, and what they mean for an attack. -- blocks = what the defence stops: "weapon", "venom", "all" or an aff name D.defs = { shield = { blocks = "all", desc = "magical shield (tattoo)" }, rebounding = { blocks = "weapon", desc = "aura of rebounding" }, fangbarrier = { blocks = "venom", desc = "sileris/fangbarrier" }, insomnia = { blocks = "asleep", desc = "insomnia" }, deafness = { blocks = "deafness", desc = "deaf defence" }, blindness = { blocks = "blindness", desc = "blind defence" }, speed = { blocks = "aeon", desc = "speed" }, }
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- -- Active and passive cures other people use. Lines are from AW's old system -- (seen in play). When one fires, AR waits for the prompt: if a specific cure -- message shows up first (guilt lifted, lovers cleared...) that's what it -- cured, otherwise AR guesses. -- cures = list (in the order we guess), "any", or nil -- count = how many it cures (default 1) -- proves = afflictions they can't have had to use it (corrects old guesses) -- cd = cooldown in seconds, for "outs" on a lock -- classes = who has it (used when you know the enemy's class) -- passive = true: not something they choose, never listed as an "out" -- patterns = lines; %t is the person's name D.class_cures = { -- class lists and cooldowns checked against the wiki's skill pages -- (Kaido, Striking, Discipline, Valour, Malignity, Dominion); fitness -- only costs 3s of balance, so it's ready again almost at once fitness = { cures = { "asthma" }, proves = { "weariness" }, cd = 3, classes = { "monk", "blademaster", "runewarden", "infernal", "paladin", "unnamable" }, patterns = { [[^%t draws a deep, measured breath\.$]] } }, shrugging = { cures = "any", proves = { "weariness" }, cd = 10, classes = { "serpent" }, patterns = { [[^%t hunches \w+ shoulders and lets out a soft hiss\.$]] } }, salt = { cures = "any", proves = { "stupidity" }, cd = 3, classes = { "alchemist" }, patterns = { [[^%t surrounds \w+ with a translucent achromatic aura\.$]] } }, willpower = { cures = "any", proves = { "confusion" }, cd = 15, classes = {}, patterns = { [[^A slight tightening of the eyes is the only sign %t makes that \w+ has made a great effort of will\.$]] } }, -- dragonheal can't be used with weariness + recklessness dragonheal = { cures = "any", proves = { "weariness", "recklessness" }, cd = 3, classes = { "dragon" }, unless = { "weariness", "recklessness" }, patterns = { [[^%t lets out a great keening, casting the impurities from \w+ form\.$]] } }, fool = { cures = "any", count = 3, proves = { "paralysis" }, cd = 35, classes = { "occultist", "jester" }, patterns = { [[^%t presses a tarot to \w+ forehead, producing a wan smile\.$]] } }, massage = { cures = "any", proves = { "paralysis" }, cd = 15, classes = {}, patterns = { [[^As \w+ massages key pressure points, a look of relief comes over %t's face as \w+ ailments ease\.$]] } }, perspire = { cures = "any", proves = { "haemophilia" }, cd = 15, classes = {}, patterns = { [[^Perspiration suddenly breaks out on %t's forehead\.$]] } }, restore = { cures = { "brokenleftleg", "brokenrightleg", "brokenleftarm", "brokenrightarm" }, count = 4, cd = 3, classes = { "monk" }, patterns = { [[^%t crackles with blue energy that wreathes itself about \w+ limbs\.$]] } }, exertion = { cures = { "paralysis" }, cd = 15, classes = {}, patterns = { [[^%t gives a great shout of exertion\.$]] } }, -- rage cures what bellwort cures rage = { cures = { "pacifism", "peace", "inlove", "generosity", "justice", "retribution", "timeloop" }, cd = 3, classes = { "runewarden", "infernal", "paladin", "unnamable" } }, -- Weaponmastery: every knight can shrug off paralysis on battlefury balance continuation = { cures = { "paralysis" }, cd = 7, classes = { "runewarden", "infernal", "paladin", "unnamable" } }, -- Striking: blademasters cure "pesky afflictions" for mana alleviate = { cures = "any", cd = 2.75, classes = { "blademaster" } }, -- more class self-cures from the wiki (no line known yet, so they only -- count as "outs" once you know the enemy's class; add a line with -- "ar ecure <name> pattern ^%t ...") expunge = { cures = { "impatience", "stupidity", "confusion", "dizziness", "epilepsy", "paranoia", "hallucinations", "dementia", "recklessness", "masochism", "vertigo", "agoraphobia", "claustrophobia", "loneliness", "shyness" }, cd = 3, classes = { "psion" } }, bloodboil = { cures = "any", cd = 4, classes = { "magi" } }, grovecure = { cures = "any", cd = 5, classes = { "druid", "sylvan" } }, accelerate = { cures = "any", cd = 10, classes = { "depthswalker" } }, syphon = { cures = "any", cd = 2, classes = { "apostate" } }, care = { cures = "any", cd = 2, classes = { "priest" } }, -- passive cures: a random affliction, whenever they tick passive = { cures = "any", cd = 0, passive = true, classes = {}, patterns = { [[^A soft chiming emanates from %t\.$]], [[^The guardian angel of %t shimmers and \w+ gives a sigh of relief\.$]], [[^A gentle glow surrounds %t\.$]], [[^A rune like a rising sun upon the ground flares, bathing %t with healing magic\.$]], [[^A song can be heard on the edge of hearing as the air distorts about %t\.$]], [[^A look of relief comes over %t as \w+ grows less pale\.$]], [[^A demonic crimson glow emanates from %t\.$]], [[^Magma boils up from within the rents in the strata of %t, solidifying to form new protective plates\.$]], [[^%t lets out a mighty roar\.$]], [[^The tempestuous form of %t is cleansed by a purifying breeze\.$]], [[^%t is surrounded in a cool, refreshing mist\.$]], [[^The fiery outer layers of %t fall away, turning to dust as they drift to the ground\.]], [[^Magma erupts forth from beneath the plates that cover %t\.$]], [[^Something pulses from within the chest of %t, and \w+ seems more vital\.$]], [[^The amorphous form of %t trembles, some of the liquid composing it falling away from the greater whole\.$]], [[^A shimmering curtain of golden light sweeps over %t\.$]], [[^The sanguine mist surrounding %t billows and writhes exultantly\.$]], [[^The globe of light illuminates %t with its brilliance\.$]], [[^Divine essence flares around %t\.$]], } }, }
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- -- Chance (0-100) an aff needs before AR counts it as on. Lock affs need -- more, so an uncertain one gets reapplied. Override: ar sure <aff> <n>. D.sure_default = 50 D.sure = { paralysis = 75, asthma = 75, slickness = 75, anorexia = 75, impatience = 75, }
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- -- Synonyms other systems or Achaea use. D.aff_aliases = { paralyzed = "paralysis", paralysed = "paralysis", para = "paralysis", sleep = "asleep", sleeping = "asleep", slick = "slickness", ano = "anorexia", asth = "asthma", imp = "impatience", clumsy = "clumsiness", stupid = "stupidity", sensitive = "sensitivity", deaf = "deafness", blind = "blindness", burning = "ablaze", transfixed = "transfixation", love = "inlove", lovers = "inlove", reckless = "recklessness", dizzy = "dizziness", weary = "weariness", }
-- Is this a known affliction name (from any cure list or venom)? function D.known_aff(name) if not D._known then D._known = {} local function add(list) for _, a in ipairs(list) do D._known[a] = true end end for _, l in pairs(D.herb_cures) do add(l) end for _, l in pairs(D.salve_cures) do add(l) end add(D.smoke_cures) add(D.focus_cures) for _, a in pairs(D.venoms) do if type(a) == "table" then add(a) else D._known[a] = true end end for _, a in ipairs({ "prone", "brokenleftarm", "brokenrightarm", "brokenleftleg", "brokenrightleg", "entangled", "bound", "webbed", "transfixation", "impaled", "aeon", "frozen", "shivering" }) do D._known[a] = true end end return D._known[D.canon(name)] == true end
function D.canon(name) if not name then return nil end local n = tostring(name):lower():gsub("[%s_%-]", "") return D.aff_aliases[n] or n end
function D.herb_from_text(text) for word in tostring(text):lower():gmatch("%a+") do if D.herb_words[word] then return D.herb_words[word] end end end

-- Used by the attack line triggers.
ar.LIMB = { ["right leg"] = "brokenrightleg", ["left leg"] = "brokenleftleg",
  ["right arm"] = "brokenrightarm", ["left arm"] = "brokenleftarm" }

-- IN: inventory tracking for Achaea (part of the ACS family of packages). -- -- `in` is a Lua keyword, so the namespace is the global table IN. It is also -- reachable as _G["in"] for anyone who prefers the lowercase name. In game, -- commands start with "in " ("in help"); a bare "in" is still the direction. -- -- What other packages can read (all kept current from GMCP unless noted): -- IN.inv[id] items you carry { id, name, qty, attrib, icon, ... } -- IN.room[id] items and mobs in the room -- IN.containers[id] { id, name, items = {[id] = item}, fetched = time } -- IN.wielded.left/right item tables or nil; IN.worn[id] -- IN.rift[key] { name, amount, desc } (key: "kelp", "aurum", "moss") -- IN.vials[] { id, fluid, kind, sips, months } (from ELIXLIST) -- IN.pipes[] { id, herb, puffs, lit } (from PIPELIST) -- IN.pipes_by_herb[herb] pipe id -- IN.gold, IN.bank numbers from Char.Status -- Functions: IN.count, IN.rift_count, IN.inv_count, IN.best_form, IN.has, -- IN.find, IN.vial_sips, IN.vials_of, IN.room_items, IN.pickup, IN.pickup_gold. -- Events: "IN.inv.changed"(action, item), "IN.room.changed"(action, item), -- "IN.container.changed"(id), "IN.rift.changed"(key, amount, old), -- "IN.vials.changed", "IN.pipes.changed", "IN.wield.changed"(left, right), -- "IN.gold.changed"(gold, delta), "IN.low"(key, amount, threshold).
IN = IN or {} _G["in"] = IN IN.version = "0.1.0"
IN.inv = IN.inv or {} IN.room = IN.room or {} IN.containers = IN.containers or {} IN.wielded = IN.wielded or {} IN.worn = IN.worn or {} IN.rift = IN.rift or {} IN.vials = IN.vials or {} IN.pipes = IN.pipes or {} IN.pipes_by_herb = IN.pipes_by_herb or {}
IN.defaults = { low_default = 10, -- warn when a curative in the rift drops below this low = {}, -- per item: low.kelp = 30 (0 turns the warning off) low_sips = 10, -- warn when a cure fluid's total sips drop below this prefer = "herb", -- IN.best_form tie-break: "herb" or "mineral" autogold = false, -- pick up gold that appears in the room autocontents = true, -- look inside containers you carry when inventory loads -- "in refill": how many vials of each fluid you want. Fluids not listed -- (bonus elixirs like ogre) are left alone. "in want <fluid> <n>" edits it. vial_set = { health = 1, mana = 1, immunity = 1, levitation = 1, speed = 1, frost = 1, venom = 1, mending = 1, restoration = 1, epidermal = 1, caloric = 1, mass = 1, }, refill_venoms = 1, -- vials of each venom to keep (0 = don't refill venoms) -- FILL VIAL<id> WITH <liquid> FROM RIFT|TUN. {source} is "rift" when the -- rift has that liquid, else "tun" (a shop); "in refill rift|tun" forces one. refill_cmd = "fill vial{vial} with {fluid} from {source}", }
function IN.echo(msg) acs.echo(msg, "in") end function IN.err(msg) acs.err(msg, "in") end function IN.debug(msg) acs.debug(msg, "in") end function IN.send(cmd) acs.send(cmd) end
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- -- Curative names. Rift names from GMCP can be long ("irid moss", "prickly -- ash"); everything is keyed by the short word.
IN.herb_to_mineral = { kelp = "aurum", ginseng = "ferrum", goldenseal = "plumbum", lobelia = "argentum", ash = "stannum", bellwort = "cuprum", bloodroot = "magnesium", hawthorn = "calamine", bayberry = "arsenic", cohosh = "gypsum", kola = "quartz", moss = "potash", skullcap = "malachite", elm = "cinnabar", valerian = "realgar", } IN.mineral_to_herb = {} for h, m in pairs(IN.herb_to_mineral) do IN.mineral_to_herb[m] = h end
-- Other riftables worth recognising in inventory names. IN.extra_curatives = { "sileris", "echinacea", "pear", "myrrh", "juniper", "nightshade", "weed", "hellebore", "galingale", "lovage", "ladyslipper", "orphine", "fern" }
IN.curative_words = {} for h, m in pairs(IN.herb_to_mineral) do IN.curative_words[#IN.curative_words + 1] = h IN.curative_words[#IN.curative_words + 1] = m end for _, w in ipairs(IN.extra_curatives) do IN.curative_words[#IN.curative_words + 1] = w end table.sort(IN.curative_words, function(a, b) return #a > #b end) -- longest first
-- "piece of kelp", "irid moss", "2 slippery elm" -> "kelp", "moss", "elm" function IN.curative_key(name) if not name then return nil end local n = tostring(name):lower() for _, w in ipairs(IN.curative_words) do if n:find("%f[%a]" .. w .. "%f[%A]") then return w end end return nil end
-- Key for anything in the rift: its curative word, or the name itself. function IN.rift_key(name) return IN.curative_key(name) or tostring(name):lower() end
-- Smokables, for pipe parsing. IN.smokables = { valerian = true, elm = true, skullcap = true, realgar = true, cinnabar = true, malachite = true }
-- Fluids by type. These lists drive vial parsing and "in refill". IN.elixirs = { "health", "mana", "immunity", "levitation", "speed", "frost", "venom", "vitality", "bromides" } IN.salves = { "mending", "restoration", "epidermal", "caloric", "mass" } IN.venoms = { "xentio", "oleander", "eurypteria", "kalmia", "digitalis", "darkshade", "curare", "epteth", "prefarar", "monkshood", "euphorbia", "colocasia", "oculus", "vernalius", "epseth", "larkspur", "slike", "voyria", "delphinium", "notechis", "vardrax", "loki", "aconite", "selarnia", "gecko", "scytherus", "ciguatoxin", "camus", "sumac", "jalk" }
-- The first word found in a vial's contents names its kind. Venom names go -- first, so "the venom curare" is curare and only the elixir is "venom". IN.fluid_words = {} for _, l in ipairs({ IN.venoms, IN.elixirs, IN.salves, { "fire", "love", "sileris", "water" } }) do for _, w in ipairs(l) do IN.fluid_words[#IN.fluid_words + 1] = w end end IN.cure_fluids = { "health", "mana", "mending", "restoration", "epidermal", "caloric", "immunity", "venom" }
function IN.fluid_kind(text) local t = tostring(text or ""):lower() if t:find("empty") then return "empty" end for _, w in ipairs(IN.fluid_words) do if t:find("%f[%a]" .. w .. "%f[%A]") then return w end end t = t:gsub("^%s+", ""):gsub("%s+$", ""):gsub("^an? ", ""):gsub("^elixir of ", "") :gsub("^salve of ", ""):gsub("^tonic of ", ""):gsub("^the ", "") return t end
function IN.tonum(v) return tonumber(tostring(v or ""):gsub(",", ""), 10) end

-- PT class detection from what people do. Each entry is a regex for a line
-- that only that class produces, with the attacker's name captured first;
-- a match calls pt.observe(name, "class", class), which beats the API.
--
--   pt.class_sign([[^(\w+) whips a .+ at you\.$]], "serpent")   -- example only
--
-- Signs added here at load time are installed by pt.init(); ones added
-- later (from another package) are installed straight away.

pt.signs = pt.signs or {}

-- Fill with real lines from play: { regex, class }
pt.sign_list = {
}

function pt.install(regex, cls)
  pt.trigger(regex, function(m)
    local who = m[2]
    if who and pt.key(who) ~= pt.key(pt.me()) and (pt.is_here(who) or pt.get(who)) then
      pt.observe(who, "class", cls)
    end
  end)
end

function pt.class_sign(regex, cls)
  pt.signs[#pt.signs + 1] = { regex, cls }
  if pt._signs_installed then pt.install(regex, cls) end
end

function pt.install_signs()
  for _, s in ipairs(pt.sign_list) do pt.install(s[1], s[2]) end
  for _, s in ipairs(pt.signs) do pt.install(s[1], s[2]) end
  pt._signs_installed = true
end

-- BS battlerage: every class's abilities from the Achaea wiki (Battlerage
-- page and the class pages, Oct 2026) and HELP BATTLERAGE, and how BS picks
-- one per swing.
--
-- What the help file and wiki say that matters here:
--   * one global 1-second cooldown on all battlerage, so one per swing;
--   * rage fades 15 seconds after you last gained or used it;
--   * six abilities a class: two damage (14 and 36 rage), a shield break
--     (17), a conditional damage (25), and afflictions or utility;
--   * conditional damage only does its extra damage if the mob has one of
--     two afflictions, and no class gives itself the ones its own
--     conditional needs: they're for groups;
--   * mob afflictions (from HELP BATTLERAGE): sensitivity +33% damage taken
--     8s, amnesia misses its next 2-3 attacks, recklessness can't shield
--     15s, weakness 66% damage 7s, feared flees every couple of seconds 8s,
--     aeon 66% attack speed 6s, clumsy misses 33% 7s, inhibit doesn't heal
--     9s, charm 20% do nothing and -20% damage 7s, stun does nothing 4s.
--
-- Kinds: dmg, aff (gives `aff`), cond (needs one of `needs`), self, ally.
-- Shield breaks live in 05_classes as `shatter`.

bs.aff_secs = {
  sensitivity = 8, amnesia = 6, recklessness = 15, weakness = 7, fear = 8,
  aeon = 6, clumsiness = 7, inhibit = 9, charm = 7, stun = 4,
}
-- Afflictions that cut the damage a mob does to you.
bs.defensive_affs = { stun = 1, weakness = 2, charm = 3, aeon = 4, clumsiness = 5, amnesia = 6 }

local function dmg(cmd, cost, cd) return { cmd = cmd, cost = cost, cd = cd, kind = "dmg" } end
local function aff(cmd, cost, cd, a) return { cmd = cmd, cost = cost, cd = cd, kind = "aff", aff = a } end
local function cond(cmd, cost, cd, a, b) return { cmd = cmd, cost = cost, cd = cd, kind = "cond", needs = { a, b } } end
local function self(cmd, cost, cd) return { cmd = cmd, cost = cost, cd = cd, kind = "self" } end
local function ally(cmd, cost, cd) return { cmd = cmd, cost = cost, cd = cd, kind = "ally" } end

