      "ss.vitals",
    },
    guide = {
      "",
      "Class-agnostic curing and defence keepup, driven by GMCP. Works for every",
      "class: class skill cures (actives) and things that cure or prevent",
      "afflictions on their own (passives) are data, switched on per class, and",
      "offered automatically when GMCP shows your character has the skill.",
      "",
      "SS is the curing half of the system. Offense is the separate AR package.",
      "Both carry the same small shared core (`acs_core`), so they install side",
      "by side in any order.",
      "",
      "## Install",
      "",
      "1. If the old combined **ACS** package is installed, remove it first",
      "   (Package Manager > ACS > Uninstall). It uses the same `acs` table.",
      "2. **Toolbox > Package Manager > Install**, pick `build/SS.mpackage`.",
      "   You should see `[ss] SS curing v0.5.0 loaded`. Type `ss help`.",
      "",
      "Rebuild after editing `src/`: `python3 build.py` (it copies in the current",
      "shared core from `../achaea-shared/`). Offline tests: `lua5.1 tests/test_ss.lua`.",
      "",
      "## First-time setup",
      "",
      "1. `ss status`: your class, balances and vitals should show.",
      "2. Mode. `ss mode server` (default): Achaea's serverside curing cures.",
      "   SS pushes your priorities, defences and sip/moss thresholds (`ss sync`)",
      "   and adds what serverside can't do: class active cures.",
      "   `ss mode client`: SS sends every cure itself, using the cure GMCP gives",
      "   for each affliction, with tree, focus and class actives as fallbacks.",
      "3. For each class: `ss defs`, and click the defences you want (see",
      "   \"Defup and keepup\" below).",
      "4. `ss active list` and `ss passive list` show what this character can use.",
      "   Anything marked n/a wasn't found in your skills. Turn things on or off",
      "   per class with `ss active on|off|auto <name>`.",
      "5. Priorities: `ss prio <aff> <1-25>`, profiles with `ss profile copy <name>`,",
      "   and `ss profile class` to use the current profile whenever you're this class.",
      "",
      "`acs dry on` shows what would be sent without sending (covers every package).",
      "",
      "## The priority table",
      "",
      "Serverside priorities come from one live table, aff -> priority (1 is",
      "cured first). Nothing is swapped in and later put back. Every time",
      "something changes, and once a second regardless, SS works the whole table",
      "out again from where you are right now, and sends serverside only what",
      "differs from what it last told it. A missed swap-back can't leave",
      "paralysis at the wrong number, because there's no swap-back to miss.",
      "Tables stack like this, with later ones winning:",
      "",
      "1. **Base**: the defaults plus your saved profile (`ss prio <aff> <n>`).",
      "2. **Your class**: the class script's table, then its subclass's, then",
      "   yours (`ss cprio <aff> <n|clear>`). This is about what you can cure",
      "   yourself: weariness higher for a class with fitness, for example.",
      "3. **Your opponent's class (vs)**: the `against` block in the script of",
      "   the class that's hitting you, its subclass's, then yours (`ss vprio",
      "   <aff> <n|clear>`). This is about how that class kills you.",
      "4. **Situations**: tables for when you're in a certain spot, your class's",
      "   (`ss sit`) and then the opponent's (`ss sit vs`). Each one has a name,",
      "   a `when`, and priorities. They're listed in order, and when two are on",
      "   at once, the later one wins.",
      "5. **By hand**: `ss swap in <name>`, `ss.prio.set()`, or a script's",
      "   `ss.prio.swap_in()`. These stay on until taken off.",
      "6. **Paralysis hold** (below).",
      "",
      "In a class script:",
      "",
      "    prios = { weariness = 6 },",
      "    situations = {",
      "      { name = \"locked\", when = { \"asthma\", \"slickness\", \"anorexia|impatience\" }, prios = { ... } },",
      "      { name = \"shielded\", when = { \"shield\" }, prios = { paralysis = 25 } },",
      "    },",
      "    against = {                  -- when someone of this class is hitting you",
      "      prios = { asthma = 2 },",
      "      situations = {",
      "        { name = \"phlegm\", when = { \"phlegmatic>=6&!has:fitness|phlegmatic>=8\", \"asthma|impatience\" },",
      "          prios = { asthma = 1, impatience = 1 } },",
      "        { name = \"aurify\", when = { \"hp<60\", \"mp<60\" }, prios = { ... } },",
      "      },",
      "      subclasses = { formulation = { prios = {}, situations = {} } },",
      "      default_sub = \"formulation\",",
      "      signs = { sublimation = { \"lua pattern\" } },  -- lines that tell the subclass",
      "    },",
      "",
      "`when` is a list where every entry has to be true. An entry can be an",
      "affliction you have or a defence you have up; `has:fitness` (a skill you",
      "have); `class:monk` (your class) or `vs:alchemist` (your opponent's);",
      "a number compared with `< <= > >= =`: stacks of an affliction (the humours",
      "by their short names, so `phlegmatic>=6`) or `hp` / `mp` in percent. `!x`",
      "is not, `a|b` either, and `a&b` both inside an either, so",
      "`phlegmatic>=6&!has:fitness|phlegmatic>=8` means 6, or 8 if you have",
      "fitness. It can also be a function. Situations from `ss.data.situations`",
      "apply to every class, under the class's own. A situation can also want",
      "defences up while it's on: `defs = { curseward = 1 }` (against an Apostate",
      "with manaleech stuck).",
      "",
      "* `ss sit` lists this class's situations, with the ones on now in yellow.",
      "  `ss sit <name> when <a> [b ...]` and `ss sit <name> <aff> <prio|clear>`",
      "  make your own. Using a scripted one's name copies it and replaces it.",
      "  `ss sit <name> off|on` skips a situation or uses it again, and",
      "  `ss sit <name> del` deletes one of yours. `ss sit general ...` does the",
      "  same for every class.",
      "* **Group fights**: when more than one person has hit you in the last",
      "  15s, the opponent tables, every situation and the paralysis hold are",
      "  off, and your class table is all that applies, so you just stand, fight and cure paralysis. There",
      "  are no separate group tables. `ss group` shows whether you're in one;",
      "  `ss group auto|on|off`, `ss group size <n>` and `ss group window <sec>`",
      "  change when it applies.",
      "* **Opponent**: one on one, it's whoever hit you last whose class is",
      "  known (people tracker or the Achaea API). The subclass comes from the",
      "  people tracker, a `signs` line, or the script's `default_sub`. `ss vs`",
      "  shows it with its tables; `ss vs <class> [subclass]` sets one by hand,",
      "  `ss vs sub <subclass>` sets just the subclass, `ss vs auto` goes back to",
      "  who's hitting you. Humour levels come from GMCP (`temperedphlegmatic",
      "  (6)`); that format still needs seeing in game.",
      "* A line shows each time situations come on or go off",
      "  (`ss prioecho on|off`).",
      "* A `CURING PRIORITY <aff> <n>` you type, or another script sends, is put",
      "  back to the table's number on the next flush.",
      "",
      "Changes go out on every heartbeat (or every prompt when HB isn't",
      "installed), up to 50 pairs per `CURING PRIORITY` command",
      "(`ss prio batch <n>`). Curing sets and PRIOAFF aren't used.",
      "`ss sync full` resends the whole table.",
      "",
      "Achaea allows `CURING PRIORITY` at most 5 times a second (ANNOUNCE NEWS",
      "#5450). Health/mana swaps and viewing (`LIST`) don't count. SS keeps",
      "under that for every priority command it sends, affliction and defence",
      "alike, and also counts the ones you type or other scripts send. When a",
      "burst is over the limit, the most urgent changes (lowest numbers) go out",
      "first. The rest wait for the next beat with room and go out with whatever",
      "the table says by then, so a priority that changed again in the meantime",
      "is never sent with its old value. A full resend of the default table is",
      "two commands, so it still goes out at once.",
      "",
      "## Class scripts",
      "",
      "`src/classes/` has one script per class, 21 classes plus Dragon and the",
      "Elemental Lords, each with slots for its subclasses (Weaponmastery",
      "specialisations for Paladin, Runewarden, Infernal and Unnamable; Tekura",
      "and Shikudo for Monk; Formulation and Sublimation for Alchemist; colours",
      "for Dragon; the four Lords). They're empty on purpose, to fill in one",
      "class at a time. Each can hold priorities, actives, passives, defence",
      "commands, a subclass detector and enter/leave/tick hooks; the field list",
      "is at the bottom of `src/02_classes.lua`. `ss subclass <name>` picks your",
      "subclass by hand until a script can detect it.",
      "",
      "## Actives and passives",
      "",
      "* **Actives** are things you do: fitness for asthma, restore for limbs,",
      "  transmute for health, tarot fool for a stack of afflictions. Each one",
      "  has a command, the balance it needs, a cooldown, and what it's for",
      "  (specific afflictions, `any` when several are waiting, or `health`/`mana`",
      "  under a threshold). One that fails with an affliction (bloodboil with",
      "  haemophilia, dragonheal with weariness and recklessness) waits until it's",
      "  gone. Classes and balances were checked against the wiki skill pages.",
      "  Add your own:",
      "  `ss active add <name> <bal> <cd> <command>`, then",
      "  `ss active cures <name> <aff> ...`.",
      "* **Passives** cure or prevent afflictions without you acting. While one",
      "  is in effect SS stops spending curatives on its afflictions (`ignore`), or",
      "  waits a few seconds first (`delay`). A passive is usually tied to a",
      "  defence, so it counts whenever that defence is up:",
      "  `ss passive add <name> <def|always> <ignore|delay> <aff> ...`.",
      "* Starter entries are in `src/02_classes.lua`. `ss.data.classes.<class>`",
      "  lists each class's actives and passives for the offense package to use.",
      "",
      "## Other things SS handles",
      "",
      "* Afflictions, cures and blockers come from the shared reference",
      "  (`achaea-shared/afflictions.lua`, 200 afflictions from the 2026 wiki),",
      "  bundled into the package. The cure GMCP sends is always tried first.",
      "  SS knows what blocks each kind of cure: anorexia stops eating,",
      "  impatience and sandfever stop focus, focusing is avoided while it would",
      "  hurt you (fulminated, guilt), hypothermia has to go before frozen,",
      "  diminished stops class active cures, and sleep allows only waking.",
      "* In client mode, defence commands come from the shared defence reference",
      "  (`achaea-shared/defences.lua`) when you haven't set one",
      "  (`ss defcmd <def> <command>[@bal]`). Passive defences (tattoos,",
      "  always-on effects) are never \"raised\".",
      "",
      "* Afflictions with the same name as a defence you keep up (blindness,",
      "  deafness, insomnia) are left alone, since GMCP lists them as both. Turn",
      "  that off with `ss defaffs off`.",
      "* When the rift shows you're out of an herb, SS eats the mineral form",
      "  instead. If the inventory package (IN) is installed, it decides.",
      "* `ss ignore <aff>` never spends cures on an affliction.",
      "* `ss predict <aff>` tells serverside about an affliction GMCP hasn't shown.",
      "* `ss focus on|off`, `ss tree on|off`, `ss clot <n>` and `ss transmute`",
      "  are synced to serverside.",
      "* `ss options` shows and sets the rest of the serverside options: insomnia",
      "  and reporting (on by default), focus with guilt / fulminated (off),",
      "  rejection and aeonlikeret (left alone until you set them), and clotto.",
      "  `ss options preempt <def>` makes a kept-up defence go ahead of the",
      "  curing queue (CURING PRIORITY DEFENCE ... PREEMPT).",
      "* Clotting won't kill you: `ss clot mana <pct>` (CURING MANATHRESHOLD,",
      "  default 40) stops clotting below that much mana, and `ss clot health",
      "  <pct>` (CURING CLOTHEALTH, default 80) clots with corrupted humours only",
      "  above that much health. An opponent's script can raise the mana floor",
      "  while you fight them: against an Alchemist it's 61, above aurification.",
      "",
      "## Defup and keepup",
      "",
      "Every class has two tables of defences, each defence with a serverside",
      "priority (1-25, 1 raised first, 25 by default):",
      "",
      "* **keepup**: kept up all the time.",
      "* **defup**: raised when you type `ss defup`, then left to drop. SS gives",
      "  serverside the defence until it comes up, then resets it.",
      "",
      "They choose from the defence lists in `src/02_classes.lua`: general ones",
      "anyone can have, the class's own, and its weapon specialisation's",
      "(dual cutting: blademastery, two handed: deflect). `ss defs [class]` shows",
      "them all as a grid. Click a name to cycle it white (neither), red (defup),",
      "orange (keepup); `U` and `D` move its priority, the number puts it back to",
      "25, and a green `*` means it's up now. The same by typing:",
      "`ss keepup|defup add|del <def> [prio]`, `ss defprio <def> <n>`,",
      "`ss keepup learn` (add what you have up now).",
      "",
      "* **Toggles** (rebounding, shield, curseward, endure): `ss deftoggle <def>",
      "  [on|off]` keeps one up while it's on, whatever the class, and wins over",
      "  keepup. Endure starts on.",
      "* **Before defup**: `ss predefup wear armour|wield shield|morph jaguar`",
      "  sets commands sent first, per class. Sentinel starts with AW's.",
      "* `ss defup stop` stops raising defup defences that haven't come up.",
      "  Changing class does too.",
      "* `Gained` / `Lost` lines for your defences: `ss defecho on|off`.",
      "* `ss keepup off` switches defup and keepup off.",
      "",
      "In server mode all of this goes to serverside as",
      "`CURING PRIORITY DEFENCE <def> <prio> <def> <prio> ...`, only what changed",
      "and up to 50 pairs a command, within the same 5-a-second limit as",
      "affliction priorities. In client mode SS raises missing defences itself.",
      "",
      "## Paralysis hold",
      "",
      "While you're paralysed and off balance, paralysis doesn't stop you doing",
      "anything yet. So if balance isn't back for longer than one more herb",
      "balance (1.5s, plus 0.3s lag and 0.2s slack), and you have something else",
      "to eat for, SS drops paralysis to 25 and eats for that first. Paralysis",
      "goes back to its own priority 2s before balance is due, so it's eaten in",
      "time, and at once if balance comes back early, paralysis is cured, or",
      "nothing else needs eating. Works in both modes.",
      "",
      "* How long until you can act comes from the game's line",
      "  (`Balance used: 0.9s.`, `Equilibrium used: 3.00s.`). For actions that",
      "  don't show one, SS learns the time per command and class from GMCP",
      "  (`ss baltimes`, `ss baltimes clear`).",
      "* Some times run long: restoring with broken limbs, tumbling with damaged",
      "  ones, confusion, lethargy. While you have any of those (broken, damaged",
      "  or mangled limbs, confusion, lethargy), the game's line still counts for",
      "  that balance, but nothing is learned, so your usual times stay usual.",
      "  Without a line SS uses the usual time, which only ever puts paralysis",
      "  back early, never late.",
      "* `ss parahold on|off`; `ss parahold balance|eq|both` says what this class",
      "  needs to act (balance by default; `both` holds only while both are gone).",
      "* Not held while a situation with `hold = false` is on",
      "  (`ss sit <name> hold off`), or while you're executing someone.",
      "",
      "## Executing someone",
      "",
      "While you're executing someone, `ss exec [secs]` puts paralysis at 1 and",
      "drops anything else at 1 to 2, and paralysis isn't held, so you're never",
      "chasing herb balance on a kill that can't wait. It's on in group fights",
      "too. It ends after `ss exec time <secs>` (8 by default), on `ss exec off`,",
      "or on \"You have slain\". Call `ss.exec.start()` / `ss.exec.stop()` from your",
      "kill alias, or list your class's lines under `exec_lines` /",
      "`exec_end_lines` in its class script.",
      "",
      "## Your limbs",
      "",
      "`ss limbs` shows how close each limb is to breaking. Each hit adds its",
      "percent (the line's, or the opponent script's `limb_hit`: a Bard is 21%),",
      "and limb afflictions set it (broken 100, damaged 200, mangled 300). Hits",
      "fade after 120 seconds. Situations can use `leftleg>=79`, `limb>=79` (the",
      "highest) and `breaks>=1`. Hit lines go in a class script under",
      "`against.limb_lines`; `ss limbs hit <limb> [pct]` counts one by hand.",
      "Situations can also compare cures: `goldenseal<kelp` is how many of your",
      "afflictions each one cures.",
      "",
      "## Fake applying and pre-applying",
      "",
      "- **Fake apply** (`ss fake legs`): `apply mending` to a broken limb. The room",
      "  doesn't see which salve, so it looks like restoration, and the real",
      "  restoration goes where it's needed. At most once every 20 seconds.",
      "- **Pre-apply** (`ss preapply head`): `apply restoration` before the limb is",
      "  damaged. It resolves 4s later, so a break in between is fixed then.",
      "- Situations ask for them with `fake = \"legs\"` and `preapply = \"head\"`",
      "  (`preapply_salve = \"mending\"` for mending), sent as soon as salve balance",
      "  is up. A situation that fakes should hold that limb's afflictions at 26,",
      "  which serverside leaves alone, or serverside restores the limb itself.",
      "- Used now: SNB disembowel, DWB assault head, Sylvan torso prepped and",
      "  blackout, Druid arms after a leg, Priest legs on inquisition, Jester mending",
      "  to torso when deafness is stripped (`flag:lost_deafness`).",
      "",
      "## Who is hitting you",
      "",
      "Attack lines from AW's old SS (`src/14_class_lines.lua`) fill in an",
      "attacker's class, and sometimes subclass (Tekura or Shikudo, which Elemental",
      "Lord), when the people tracker doesn't know it.",
      "",
      "SS lists everyone who has hit you in the last 30 seconds, with their class",
      "and city: `ss attackers` (also shown in `ss ui`). Someone stays on the list",
      "until 30s pass with no new hit from them (`ss attackers window <sec>`).",
      "",
      "It works for any class without knowing their attack lines. A line that",
      "starts with a player's name and mentions you counts as a hit when it comes",
      "with harm within half a second: lost health or mana, a new affliction, or a",
      "lost defence. The afflictions that came with each hit are listed against",
      "that person. Friendly lines (says, bows, waves...) are skipped; add a word",
      "with `ss attackers skip <word>`. `ss attackers harm off` counts every such",
      "line from someone in the room, harm or not.",
      "",
      "Class and city come from the people tracker (PT) if it's installed: what PT",
      "saw them do first, otherwise the Achaea API, looked up on their first hit.",
      "Without PT they show as `?`. Expiry runs on the heartbeat (HB) if it's",
      "installed, otherwise on SS's own one-second timer.",
      "",
      "## For other packages",
      "",
      "Read only: `ss.affs`, `ss.has(aff)`, `ss.defs`, `ss.def_up(def)`,",
      "`ss.bals.balance`, `ss.bals.equilibrium`, `ss.bals.herb` (and salve, smoke,",
      "sip, moss, focus, tree), `ss.vitals`, `ss.skills`. Events: `ss.aff.gained`,",
      "`ss.aff.lost`, `ss.def.up`, `ss.def.down`, `ss.balance`(name, available),",
      "`ss.vitals`, `ss.tick`.",
      "",
      "Defences: `ss.keepup.wanted()` (def -> priority SS wants kept up now),",
      "`ss.keepup.list()` (everything this class raises), `ss.keepup.missing()`,",
      "`ss.data.def_lists[class]`; event `ss.def.toggle`(def, on).",
      "",
      "Priorities: `ss.prio.get(aff)`, `ss.prio.table()`, `ss.prio.active_names()`",
      "(\"group fight\", situations, swaps by hand, parahold on now),",
      "`ss.prio.group()`; event `ss.prio.swapped`(name, on) when a situation or",
      "\"group fight\" comes on or goes off.",
      "",
      "Attackers: `ss.attackers.list()`, `ss.attackers.get(name)` giving",
      "`{ name, class, city, hits, first, last, affs }`; events `ss.attacker.hit`(name, record),",
      "`ss.attacker.expired`(name), `ss.attackers.changed`.",
      "",
      "## Check these in game",
      "",
      "Serverside command wording now matches HELP CURINGSYSTEM (notes in",
      "`docs/combat-help-notes.md`). Still not run on a live character:",
      "",
      "* Active cure commands and cooldowns in `src/02_classes.lua` (`AB <skill>`).",
      "* Balance lines in `src/99_init.lua` (the `Balance used` / `Equilibrium",
      "  used` lines are AW's, from the game): the \"You may ... another\" recovery",
      "  lines, and the eat/apply/drink/smoke/focus/tree lines that mark a balance",
      "  used (so SS knows your balances under serverside curing too). If a",
      "  recovery line doesn't match, the balance still comes back after its time,",
      "  just a moment later. Balance times (from AW) are in `ss.bal_timeouts`.",
      "",
      "* Limb hit lines (none yet) and the limb affliction levels in",
      "  `src/12_limbs.lua` (head and torso one level lower, guessed).",
      "",
      "## Files",
      "",
      "| File | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `src/00_acs_core.lua` | shared core (copied from `achaea-shared/` by the build) |",
      "| `src/00b_afflictions.lua`, `src/00c_defences.lua` | shared references (copied by the build) |",
      "| `src/01_data.lua` | afflictions, cures, priorities, general defences |",
      "| `src/02_classes.lua` | class actives, passives, defence lists by class |",
      "| `src/03_state.lua` | settings and GMCP state: vitals, balances, affs, defs, skills, rift |",
      "| `src/classes/*.lua` | one script per class, to fill in |",
      "| `src/04_engine.lua` | cure engine (client mode, and class actives) |",
      "| `src/04_prio.lua` | the live priority table and swaps |",
      "| `src/05_keepup.lua` | defup and keepup, per class |",
      "| `src/06_server.lua` | serverside curing sync |",
      "| `src/07_commands.lua` | `ss` commands |",
      "| `src/08_ui.lua` | optional status window (`ss ui`) |",
      "| `src/09_attackers.lua` | who is hitting you |",
      "| `src/10_parahold.lua` | paralysis hold and balance times |",
      "| `src/11_opponent.lua` | who you're fighting, for the vs tables (`ss vs`, `ss vprio`) |",
      "| `src/12_limbs.lua` | your own limb damage (`ss limbs`) |",
      "| `src/13_execute.lua` | executing someone: paralysis first (`ss exec`) |",
      "| `src/14_class_lines.lua` | attack lines that give away a class (AW's old triggers), DIAGNOSE humour counts, predict lines |",
      "| `src/15_salves.lua` | fake applying and pre-applying (`ss fake`, `ss preapply`) |",
      "| `src/99_init.lua` | wiring |",
    },
  },
