    },
    guide = {
      "",
      "The offense half of the system; curing is SS. AR works for any class. It",
      "tracks what your target is afflicted with, watches them cure, knows their",
      "locks and defences, confirms your hits from the game's own lines, and runs",
      "the attack module for whatever class you're playing. It installs alone or",
      "next to SS (they share `acs_core`, newest copy wins).",
      "",
      "## Install",
      "",
      "Mudlet: **Toolbox > Package Manager > Install** `build/AR.mpackage`.",
      "You should see `[ar] loaded v0.5.0`.",
      "",
      "Rebuild after editing `src/`: `python3 build.py`.",
      "Tests: `python3 tests/run_tests.py` (needs `pip install lupa`).",
      "",
      "## Everyday use",
      "",
      "| Type | Does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `t <name>` | target someone (also sets the in-game target) |",
      "| `tc` | clear target |",
      "| `k` | attack with your class's module |",
      "| `ar ta` | target status: afflictions, defences, lock, their cure balances, class cures ready |",
      "| `ar give <affs>` / `ar cure <affs>` | fix the tracker by hand |",
      "| `ar reset` | forget everything about the target |",
      "| `ar def shield up` | mark a defence by hand |",
      "| `ar eclass <class>` | say what class they are |",
      "| `ar sure [aff n]` | chance an aff needs to count as on (lock affs default to 75) |",
      "| `ar lines [off\\|on class]` | attack lines loaded per class |",
      "| `ar people` | everyone being tracked and what they have |",
      "| `ar follow <name>` | take party `TARGET x` calls from that person (`ar follow off` to stop) |",
      "| `ar dry` is `acs dry` | dry run covers both packages |",
      "",
      "A status line prints when the target's state changes (`ar show off` to stop).",
      "",
      "## How tracking stays honest",
      "",
      "* **Chances, not guesses.** Every aff has a chance from 0 to 100. A cure",
      "  you can't see is random in Achaea, so eating kelp with asthma and",
      "  weariness puts both at 50. Lock affs need 75 to count, so an uncertain",
      "  asthma gets reapplied. The status line shows uncertain ones greyed with",
      "  their chance.",
      "* **Attack lines from your old triggers.** About 385 lines from every class",
      "  (yours and allies') afflict whoever they name, strip defences, and note",
      "  the attacker's class. See `notes/old-triggers-left.md` for the class",
      "  logic still to move into modules.",
      "* **Everyone, not just the target.** Anyone you've targeted keeps their own",
      "  record, so cures you see from them while you hit someone else still count,",
      "  and switching back picks up where you left off.",
      "* **Cures settle at the prompt.** An eat/apply/smoke waits for the prompt, so",
      "  a specific cure line on the same tick (\"looks less guilty\", unweaving lines",
      "  and so on) wins over the guess. `** Illusion **` undoes the tick.",
      "* **Backtracking.** When something proves they *don't* have an aff (standing",
      "  up means no paralysis, fitness means no weariness, holding breath means no",
      "  asthma, parrying means no nausea, applying sileris means no slickness), AR",
      "  drops it, and the share of the last random cure it took moves onto the",
      "  other affs.",
      "* **Their cures.** Eating, applying, smoking, focusing and tree touches by",
      "  your target remove the affliction they most likely cured, in serverside",
      "  priority order. Each also proves something: someone who eats can't have",
      "  anorexia, someone who smokes can't have asthma, and so on.",
      "* **Their balances.** AR times their eat/apply/smoke/focus/tree balances,",
      "  so `ar ta` shows when they can cure again. Tune with `ar ebal`.",
      "* **Their class cures.** Fitness, dragonheal, shrugging and the like are",
      "  in `ar ecure list`. When a lock is real but a class cure is ready, the",
      "  status shows \"outs: fitness\". These use the real lines from your old",
      "  triggers, plus the passive cure lines; fix one with",
      "  `ar ecure fitness pattern ^%t ...`.",
      "* **Defences.** Shield, rebounding, fangbarrier, insomnia, deaf and blind",
      "  are tracked, and modules strip them first.",
      "",
      "## Hit confirmation",
      "",
      "Modules tell AR what an attack should do. AR waits for the result:",
      "",
      "* Parry, dodge, miss, reflection, rebounding or shield lines cancel it",
      "  (the real lines from your old system).",
      "* Limb damage you deal (\"As you carve into...\") and party \"Hit X limb for",
      "  N%\" calls add up per limb in `ar ta`. Party \"kalmia gecko on X\" and",
      "  \"Afflicted X: ...\" calls afflict X. \"You have slain X\" resets X.",
      "* A fangbarrier line keeps the hit but drops the venoms.",
      "* A **hit line** confirms it. Teach one per attack: `ar learn dstab`, then",
      "  attack. The next line naming your target is saved for that class.",
      "  `ar hitlines` shows them, `ar log` shows recent results.",
      "* With no hit line yet, an attack that fired (you lost balance) and wasn't",
      "  cancelled counts as a hit. Turn this off with `ar optimistic off`.",
      "",
      "## Any class, any ability",
      "",
      "* `ar affline add <regex with %t> = aff1 aff2 -curedaff` makes any line",
      "  afflict or cure the target. Use it for class abilities without a module.",
      "* `ar sign add <class> <regex with %p>` or `ar sign learn <class> <person>`",
      "  teaches AR a line that shows someone's class. Classes seen in combat beat",
      "  the people tracker's API class, and AR reports them back to it.",
      "",
      "## Class modules (all classes + Dragon)",
      "",
      "`k` runs the module for your current class. Each one strips the defence",
      "blocking it, uses a kill move when AR can see the condition, and otherwise",
      "stacks the lock afflictions that class can give. `k <move>` forces a named",
      "move, for example `k devour`, `k rub` or `k catastrophe`.",
      "",
      "| Class | What `k` does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| Jester | aeon, then moon card with a named aff, hangedman, lovers, vent; badjoke strips; bop when nothing's left. `k rub` / `k death` for the Death card |",
      "| Occultist | instill on eq and a tarot card on balance in the same round; gremlin strips shields |",
      "| Serpent | doublestab down the venom lock; flay strips; bite voyria at true lock |",
      "| Runewarden, Paladin, Infernal, Unnamable | weapon style set with `ar style dualcut\\|dualblunt\\|twohanded\\|snb`. DSL/slaughter/slice venoms, raze/fracture/carve strips. Runewarden bisects at 20% health |",
      "| Apostate | stares, two at a time with deadeyes |",
      "| Shaman | curses, two at a time with jinx |",
      "| Alchemist | tempers the right humour, then wrack or truewrack; educe copper strips; aurify at 60% health (it can't see their mana) |",
      "| Magi | bombard, mudslide, dehydrate, transfix, fulminate, conflagrate; destroy at 40% with conflagration |",
      "| Sylvan | static, hailstone, cyclone, razorwind, thunderclap, flash, thornrend venoms; shear strips |",
      "| Psion | weave deathblow, puncture, sever, backhand, exsanguinate, overhand, entwine; weave cleave strips |",
      "| Pariah | logographs: serpent, jackal, skein, scales, nest, sun, bear, scarab; fissure strips |",
      "| Priest | zeal verses on prayer balance plus angel sear/shine on eq; angel strip, hunt heresy |",
      "| Depthswalker | aeon, then shadow reap venoms; shadow strike breaks shields |",
      "| Sentinel | spear thrust venoms, doublestrike, gouge, lacerate; rive strips |",
      "| Blademaster | strike to neck/throat/stomach/ears/shoulder/temple/eyes/knees; flamefist strips rebounding |",
      "| Monk | tekura combos with palmstrike/bladehand; roundhouse strips |",
      "| Druid | basilisk gaze and glare; negate strips |",
      "| Bard | punctuate strips, highsun attacks. Bladedance depends on your position in the dance, which AR doesn't track yet |",
      "| Dragon | rend with claw venoms; tailsmash and breathstrip strip; `k devour` |",
      "",
      "The abilities come from the Achaea wiki (October 2026). The routines are",
      "starting points, not tested in play. Some effects are named from the",
      "skill's description rather than a stated affliction, mainly Blademaster",
      "strikes and the Monk combo. Expect to adjust the order for your own fights.",
      "",
      "## Writing a class module",
      "",
      "Most modules are data for `ar.offense.simple` (see `src/09_builder.lua`",
      "and `src/11_classes.lua`). For full control, see `src/10_serpent.lua`. Register a table with `attack(target, args)`.",
      "Pick afflictions with `ar.offense.next_aff(list)` or",
      "`ar.offense.next_venoms(list, n)`, strip defences found by",
      "`ar.offense.blocker()`, send with `ar.queue(cmd)`, and call",
      "`ar.hits.expect{ key = \"dstab\", venoms = {...}, affs = {...} }` so AR can",
      "track it.",
      "",
      "## Check in game",
      "",
      "Written from knowledge of Achaea and not yet tested live, so confirm early:",
      "",
      "* The cure lines in `src/04_watch.lua` (eat/apply/smoke/focus/tree).",
      "* The miss and fangbarrier lines in `src/05_hits.lua`.",
      "* The class cure patterns (`ar ecure list`).",
    },
  },
