    events = { "bs.clear", "bs.fled", "bs.killed", "bs.started", "bs.stopped", "bs.target", "bs.warn" },
    guide = {
      "",
      "PvE hunting for any class, built from AW's old `pve` scripts. Built on the",
      "shared ACS core, so it installs side by side with SS (curing), AR (offense),",
      "QM (queue), RM (rooms) and PT (people).",
      "",
      "## Install",
      "",
      "Mudlet: **Toolbox > Package Manager > Install**, pick `build/BS.mpackage`",
      "(or the Achaea bundle, which includes it). Turn off the old `pve` folders",
      "first, or both will attack. Rebuild after editing `src/` with",
      "`python3 build.py`; offline tests: `lua5.1 tests/test_bs.lua`.",
      "",
      "## Use",
      "",
      "1. In a hunting area, `bs room` (or `bget`) lists the mobs. Click one to add",
      "   it to the area's list (green = listed; click again to remove). Or type",
      "   `bs add knight`. Part of the name is enough. Order matters: `bs up`,",
      "   `bs list`.",
      "2. `bs` (or `bstart` / `bstop`) turns hunting on and off. It stays on while",
      "   you walk, and attacks whatever's listed in each room you walk into.",
      "   `bs stayon off` stops it at the end of each room instead.",
      "",
      "You do the walking: Achaea's rules forbid automating gold and XP gathering,",
      "so BS never moves you.",
      "",
      "## How a swing works (as in pve)",
      "",
      "Each swing is one game alias, put on the server queue (`freestand`, as pve",
      "did), so it fires the moment balance comes back:",
      "",
      "`stand / wield <weapons> / <rage ability> / <attack>`",
      "",
      "* **Attack** is per class, ported from pve: Jester `bop`, then",
      "  `gallowshumour` under 50% target health; knights follow your spec from",
      "  GMCP (dual cutting `dsl`, sword and shield `combination`, two handed",
      "  `battlefury/slaughter`, dual blunt `doublewhirl`); Bard goes into heart's",
      "  fury first, Blademaster into arash; Sentinel and Occultist change with the",
      "  target's health; Shaman jinxes when the jinx line says it can; Psion uses",
      "  transcendence. All of it is in `src/05_classes.lua`.",
      "* **Shields**: when a mob's shield goes up (pve's trigger lines), the swing",
      "  uses the class's shield-breaking rage ability plus the attack if you have",
      "  17 rage (Jester: `throw jacks`), otherwise the raze (Jester: `badjoke`).",
      "  Shaman and Apostate attack through shields, so they ignore them.",
      "  If another listed mob in the room has no shield, BS switches to it, and",
      "  goes back to the first one as soon as a line says its shield is down (it",
      "  attacked you, or the shield faded). With nothing else to hit, it razes.",
      "* **Rage** (`src/07_rage.lua`): every class's six abilities from the wiki,",
      "  tagged damage / affliction / conditional / shield break / self. One per",
      "  swing (there's a 1s global cooldown), picked by situation:",
      "  nothing on a mob under 15% (`bs rage low`); when you're under 60%",
      "  (`bs rage defend`), a stun/weakness/charm/aeon/clumsy/amnesia or a self",
      "  ability first; sensitivity first when your class has it (+33% damage);",
      "  otherwise the biggest damage ability you can afford. Conditionals only fire",
      "  when the mob has the affliction they need (no class gives its own, so solo",
      "  they stay unused). Fear is off (`bs rage fear on`): a feared mob runs.",
      "  `bs rage extra inhibit` and the like add other afflictions. The cooldown",
      "  starts when the game runs the swing.",
      "* **Weapons**: pve's wield list per class (`shield, blackjack` for Jester).",
      "* QM sends the SETALIAS and QUEUE when it's loaded; otherwise BS does",
      "  (`setalias bsbash ...`, `queue addclear freestand bsbash`).",
      "",
      "Change any of it for the class you're on: `bs attack`, `bs raze`,",
      "`bs shatter`, `bs wield`, `bs prep` (sent on start; Pariah has pve's",
      "epitaph prep), `bs rage add`. `bs status` shows the next swing.",
      "",
      "## Also",
      "",
      "* Gold is picked up by item id; `bs stash put sovereigns in pack` puts it",
      "  away. `bs pickup add <text>` for anything else.",
      "* Each new target gets `st <id>` (so the game reports its health);",
      "  `bs party on` also sends `pt target: <id>` (pve's `pvpt`).",
      "* Holds the swing while you're paralysed, prone, stunned, asleep, webbed,",
      "  entangled and so on, so curing goes first.",
      "* Warns at 50% health; at 30% stops and leaves the way you came in",
      "  (`bs warn`, `bs flee <pct>`, `bs flee <command>`).",
      "* Stops if someone PT counts as an enemy walks in (`bs enemy flee|ignore`).",
      "* `bs stats`: kills, gold and xp (pve's earned summary), also shown when you",
      "  stop.",
      "",
      "`bs help` has the full list. `acs dry on` echoes commands without sending.",
      "",
      "## For other packages",
      "",
      "Events: `bs.started`, `bs.stopped`(why), `bs.target`(id, name),",
      "`bs.killed`(id, name), `bs.clear`(area), `bs.warn`(hp%), `bs.fled`(why, cmd).",
      "",
      "`bs.class_attack[\"jester\"] = function(id, c) return \"bop \" .. id end` takes",
      "over the attack part for a class (`c` has hp, shield, rage, spec, stance).",
      "",
      "## Not carried over from pve",
      "",
      "* Jester juggling bookkeeping (the attack never used it).",
      "* The Fomori \"curing predict\" line: that's curing, so it belongs in SS.",
      "* The armour ids in `preBashing` (it built them but never sent them).",
      "",
      "## Check in game",
      "",
      "* Spec and stance come from GMCP charstats (`Spec: ...`, `Stance: ...`).",
      "  If `bs status` shows the wrong attack for a knight, Bard or Blademaster,",
      "  paste me your charstats.",
      "* The shield lines are pve's; a class whose raze line isn't among them",
      "  keeps razing. Paste the line and it gets added.",
      "* Kills are counted when the target leaves the room list, so a mob that",
      "  wanders off counts as a kill.",
    },
