    guide = {
      "",
      "Tracks the room you're in from GMCP: exits, denizens, items on the ground,",
      "other players, recent history, and gives other packages one API over the",
      "IRE mapping script (walking, paths, marks). Other",
      "packages (bashing `bs`, people tracker `pt`, offense `ar`...) read its",
      "state and listen to its events instead of parsing room text themselves.",
      "",
      "Built on the shared ACS core (`src/00_acs_core.lua`, an exact copy of",
      "`achaea-shared/acs_core.lua`), so it installs side by side with the other",
      "packages. `acs dry on` and `acs debug on` cover it too.",
      "",
      "## Install",
      "",
      "Mudlet: **Toolbox > Package Manager > Install**, pick `build/RM.mpackage`.",
      "You should see `[rm] loaded v0.1.0`. Type `room help`.",
      "",
      "Rebuild after editing `src/`: `python3 build.py`. Tests: `lua5.1 tests/test_rm.lua`.",
      "",
      "## Commands",
      "",
      "Commands start with `room`. The Lua root is still `rm` (`rm.room`,",
      "`rm.denizens()`...), but `rm` on its own goes to the game.",
      "",
      "| Command | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `room status` | this room: area, exits, denizens, items, players, walk progress |",
      "| `room mobs` / `room items` | denizens / ground items with ids |",
      "| `room players` | other players here (you're left out) |",
      "| `room hist [n]` | recent rooms |",
      "| `room city` | which city this area counts as |",
      "| `room city NAME\\|none\\|clear` | tag this area as a city's ground (e.g. a defendable area), as no city's, or back to the default |",
      "| `room cities` | areas you've tagged |",
      "| `room echo on\\|off` | one-line room summary after every move |",
      "| `room ui on\\|off` | room window (the GUI's room box shows the same) |",
      "| `room pickup` | auto-pickup rules, and whether it's on (see below) |",
      "| `room refresh` | ask the game for the room's item list again |",
      "",
      "Settings are saved per character in `<Mudlet home>/acs_<name>_rm.lua`.",
      "",
      "### Auto-pickup",
      "",
      "RM picks up gold and corpses as they land in the room, once you have",
      "balance and equilibrium. Anything else you can pick up gets one line the",
      "first time it shows up:",
      "",
      "    [rm] a sprig of lobelia here. Pick these up? [always] [never]",
      "",
      "Click one and it's remembered. `room items` shows everything on the ground",
      "with [get] / [skip] links, so you can change your mind later. The answers",
      "live in one file for all your characters: `<Mudlet home>/acs_pickup.lua`.",
      "",
      "| Command | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `room pickup on\\|off` | turn it on or off |",
      "| `room pickup now` | pick up everything here that's on the list |",
      "| `room pickup always NAME` / `never NAME` | same as clicking, by exact item name |",
      "| `room pickup add TEXT` / `skip TEXT` | pick up / leave anything with TEXT in its name |",
      "| `room pickup forget NAME\\|TEXT` | drop a rule |",
      "| `room pickup ask on\\|off` | stop or start the [always] [never] offers |",
      "",
      "Exact names win over text rules. What you added with `bs pickup add` is",
      "picked up too. While auto-pickup is on, bashing and `in autogold` leave",
      "picking up to RM, so nothing is grabbed twice.",
      "",
      "### The mapper does the rest",
      "",
      "RM builds on the IRE mapping script (Mudlet Mapper) and doesn't duplicate",
      "it. Use the mapper for:",
      "",
      "* walking: `goto NUM|MARK|AREA`, `mstop`, `mpp` (pause)",
      "* marks: `room mark NAME`, `room marks`, `room unmark NAME`",
      "* finding and looking: `rf TEXT` (`room find`), `rl` (`room look`, shows exits)",
      "* the map window and centring it",
      "",
      "The mapper's commands also start with `room`. When you type one of them,",
      "RM stays quiet and lets the mapper answer. RM's own command words",
      "(status, mobs, items, players, hist, city, cities, echo, ui, refresh, help)",
      "don't clash with the mapper's.",
      "",
      "## For other packages",
      "",
      "State (read only):",
      "",
      "* `rm.room`: `num, name, area, environment, coords, map, desc, exits (dir -> num), details (set)`",
      "* `rm.prev`, `rm.history` (numbers, newest first)",
      "* `rm.players`: `name -> fullname`",
      "* `rm.items`: `id -> {id, name, attrib, icon, seq}`",
      "",
      "Functions:",
      "",
      "* `rm.here()`, `rm.has_exit(dir)`, `rm.exit_list()`, `rm.dir_to(num)`, `rm.back_dir()`",
      "* `rm.player_list()`, `rm.has_player(name)`",
      "* `rm.denizens(include_protected)`: denizens in arrival order; skips `x`",
      "  (\"shouldn't be attacked\") unless asked",
      "* `rm.find_denizen({\"rat\", \"knight\"})`: first match, in list order",
      "* `rm.count_denizens(name)`, `rm.item_list()`, `rm.find_item(name|id)`, `rm.grouped(list)`",
      "* `rm.pickup_on()`, `rm.pickup_decide(item)` (\"get\" / \"skip\" / nil), `rm.pickup_set(name, act)`, `rm.pickup_now()`",
      "* `rm.area_city(area)`: city (lowercase) whose ground an area is, or nil; `rm.set_area_city(area, city)`",
      "* Mapper, through RM so packages don't each check for it:",
      "  `rm.mapper()` (is it loaded), `rm.go_to(num|mark|area, dash)`, `rm.stop()`,",
      "  `rm.walking()` (`{dest, steps_left}` or nil), `rm.path_to(to, from)`, `rm.marks()` (the mapper's marks), `rm.room_name(num)`",
      "",
      "Events (normal Mudlet events):",
      "",
      "| Event | Arguments |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `rm.moved` | num, prev_num |",
      "| `rm.area` | area, prev_area |",
      "| `rm.info` | num (every Room.Info, moved or not) |",
      "| `rm.player.entered` / `rm.player.left` | name (and fullname on entered) |",
      "| `rm.players.changed` | |",
      "| `rm.denizen.added` / `rm.denizen.removed` | id, name |",
      "| `rm.item.added` / `rm.item.removed` | id, name |",
      "| `rm.items.changed` | |",
      "| `rm.wrongdir` | dir |",
      "| `rm.pickup.sent` | id, name |",
      "| `rm.walk.start` / `rm.walk.arrived` | dest (from the mapper's `mmapper arrived`) |",
      "| `rm.walk.stop` | dest, reason: \"no path\" or \"stopped\" (`mmapper failed path` / `mmapper stopped`) |",
      "",
      "## Files",
      "",
      "| File | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `src/00_acs_core.lua` | shared ACS core (don't edit here; edit `achaea-shared/`) |",
      "| `src/01_rm.lua` | module setup, settings |",
      "| `src/02_room.lua` | Room.Info, players, history |",
      "| `src/03_items.lua` | room items and denizens (Char.Items, location \"room\") |",
      "| `src/04_map.lua` | API over the mapper (walking, paths, marks), its events as `rm.walk.*` |",
      "| `src/05_commands.lua` | `room` commands |",
      "| `src/07_pickup.lua` | auto-pickup and its `room pickup` commands |",
      "| `src/06_ui.lua` | room window (redraws on the hb heartbeat when that package is loaded) |",
      "| `src/99_init.lua` | wiring |",
      "",
      "## Check in game",
      "",
      "Written against your GMCP dump, but not run on a live character yet:",
      "",
      "* After a move, `room status` should list the new room's mobs. If items lag,",
      "  RM asks for `Char.Items.Room` itself after half a second.",
    },
  },
