    events = { "af.blocked", "af.lost", "af.moved", "af.start", "af.stop" },
    guide = {
      "",
      "Follows one person room by room, but won't walk you into trouble:",
      "",
      "* not into an **enemy city** or one of its **defendable areas**;",
      "* not into a room with a **totem** in it;",
      "* not into a room with **guards** in it (outside your own city).",
      "",
      "It squints into the room first to look for a totem or guards. If you can't",
      "squint (no skill, blind), it goes by area alone: an enemy city or its area",
      "is taken to have them, so you stay; anywhere else is taken to have none, so",
      "you follow.",
      "",
      "It doesn't use the game's FOLLOW: it watches your leader leave (\"Bob leaves",
      "to the north.\") and sends the step itself after the checks. When it stops",
      "you, it says why and waits. If your leader walks back into your room, it",
      "carries on from there.",
      "",
      "Built on the shared ACS core, so nothing is sent until you're logged in.",
      "Uses RM's room state when RM is loaded, GMCP otherwise.",
      "",
      "## Install",
      "",
      "It's in the all-in-one `Achaea.mpackage`. On its own: **Toolbox > Package",
      "Manager > Install**, pick `build/AF.mpackage`. Type `afol help`.",
      "",
      "Rebuild after editing `src/`: `python3 build.py`. Tests:",
      "`lua5.1 tests/test_af.lua`, or `pip install lupa && python3 tests/run_lua.py tests/test_af.lua`.",
      "",
      "## Commands",
      "",
      "Commands start with `afol` (`follow` and `af` are left to the game).",
      "",
      "| Command | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `afol NAME` | follow NAME (also `afol follow NAME`) |",
      "| `afol off` | stop following |",
      "| `afol` / `afol status` | who you're following, your city, enemy cities, squint |",
      "| `afol check DIR` | what would happen if your leader went DIR (squints) |",
      "| `afol squint on\\|off` | squint before stepping in (on) |",
      "| `afol guards on\\|off` | guards stop you (on); never in your own city |",
      "| `afol city NAME\\|none\\|auto` | your city; auto reads it from GMCP |",
      "| `afol enemies all\\|list` | all: every city but yours (default); list: only your enemy list |",
      "| `afol enemy CITY [off]` | add a city to (or take it off) your enemy list |",
      "| `afol area` | which city the area you're in counts as |",
      "| `afol area add CITY AREA` | AREA (or `here`) belongs to CITY: defendable areas, ports... |",
      "| `afol area add none AREA` | AREA has a city's name in it but isn't that city's |",
      "| `afol area remove AREA` | forget an area you added |",
      "| `afol areas` | the areas you've added |",
      "| `afol echo on\\|off` | a line for every step |",
      "",
      "PT's hostile cities (`ptr hostile city mhaldor`) always count as enemies.",
      "",
      "## How it decides",
      "",
      "When your leader leaves in a direction:",
      "",
      "1. The room that way is looked up on the Mudlet map. If its area belongs to",
      "   an enemy city, you stay. An area belongs to a city when its name has the",
      "   city's name in it (`Mhaldor`, `the City of Mhaldor`), or you tagged it",
      "   with RM's `room city NAME` or `afol area add`. RM's tags are checked first. A room that isn't mapped counts as the area you're in.",
      "2. Otherwise you squint that way. Squint shows every room in a line, so",
      "   only the first one (where your leader went) is read: \"totem\" in it, or a",
      "   guard word (guard, guardsman, sentry, soldier, centurion, watchman,",
      "   legionnaire...), stops you. Guards in your own city don't. The first",
      "   room ends at the next room's title when the map knows it, or after its",
      "   one description line when the game doesn't wrap lines (`config",
      "   screenwidth 0`). With wrapped lines and an unmapped next room, a title",
      "   can't be told apart from the end of a sentence, so every room seen is",
      "   checked instead.",
      "3. If the squint fails (you don't have it, you're blind, an unknown reply,",
      "   no reply in two seconds) you follow. If the game says you don't have the skill, AF stops",
      "   squinting until `afol squint on`.",
      "4. Otherwise you step after them, retrying twice if the step doesn't happen.",
      "",
      "A squint result is reused for the same room for 30 seconds.",
      "",
      "## For other scripts",
      "",
      "```lua",
      "af.start(\"Bob\"), af.stop()",
      "af.following()            -- \"Bob\" or nil",
      "af.f.state                -- \"watching\" | \"checking\" | \"moving\" | \"blocked\" | \"lost\"",
      "af.check(\"n\", function(ok, why) end)",
      "af.area_city(\"the City of Mhaldor\")  -- \"mhaldor\"",
      "af.is_enemy_city(\"mhaldor\")",
      "af.my_city()",
      "```",
      "",
      "Events: `af.start(name)`, `af.stop(name, reason)`, `af.moved(dir, num)`,",
      "`af.blocked(name, dir, reason)`, `af.lost(name)`.",
      "",
      "## Check in game",
      "",
      "Written from knowledge of Achaea, not run on a live character yet:",
      "",
      "* **Squint wording.** Matched to your screenshot (\"Narrowing your eyes,",
      "  you squint off toward the east.\" ... \"You can see no further.\"). The",
      "  \"can't squint\" lines in `af.squint_fail` (`src/03_squint.lua`) are still",
      "  guesses; if squinting fails with a message that isn't listed, paste it",
      "  and it can be added.",
      "* **Leave lines.** Anything like \"Bob leaves to the north.\" or \"Bob rides",
      "  off up.\" works (`af.leave_verbs` in `src/04_follow.lua`).",
      "* **Defendable areas.** Only areas named after a city count until you add",
      "  the rest with `room city NAME` (RM) or `afol area add`.",
      "",
      "## Files",
      "",
      "| File | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `src/00_acs_core.lua` | shared ACS core (don't edit here; edit `achaea-shared/`) |",
      "| `src/01_af.lua` | module setup, settings, room helpers |",
      "| `src/02_areas.lua` | cities, areas, enemies |",
      "| `src/03_squint.lua` | squinting for totems and guards |",
      "| `src/04_follow.lua` | watching the leader and stepping after them |",
      "| `src/05_commands.lua` | `afol` commands |",
      "| `src/99_init.lua` | wiring |",
    },
  },
