    guide = {
      "",
      "Remembers everyone you come across: city, house, class, level and kills",
      "(from the public Achaea API), race and age (from HONOURS), where and when you",
      "last saw them (from GMCP), and your own enemies, allies and other lists.",
      "Known names are coloured in game text: enemies red and underlined, allies",
      "green, everyone else by city.",
      "",
      "Built on the shared ACS core, so it installs next to the other ACS packages",
      "(curing, offense, bashing) in any order. It also works on its own.",
      "",
      "Commands start with `ptr` (plain `pt` is a game command). The Lua names",
      "other scripts use stay `pt.*`.",
      "",
      "## Install",
      "",
      "Mudlet: **Toolbox > Package Manager > Install**, pick `build/PT.mpackage`.",
      "You should see `[pt] loaded v0.1.0`. Type `ptr help`. Needs Mudlet 4.10 or",
      "newer for the API lookups (`getHTTP`).",
      "",
      "Rebuild after editing `src/`: `python3 build.py`. Tests:",
      "`lua5.1 tests/test_pt.lua`, or `pip install lupa && python3 tests/run.py`.",
      "",
      "## Everyday use",
      "",
      "* Walk around. Everyone in your room is recorded with the room and time, and",
      "  anyone new is looked up on the API in the background (one request at a time).",
      "* `ptr NAME` shows what's known. `ptr check NAME` refreshes it from the API.",
      "* `ptr here` lists your room. Arrivals and departures are echoed with city,",
      "  class and enemy/ally tags (`ptr arrivals off` to stop).",
      "* `ptr online` shows who's online, counted by city, plus enemies and allies",
      "  online. `ptr online scan` looks up everyone online you don't know yet.",
      "* Every minute PT fetches the online list (one request) and rechecks anyone",
      "  online whose record is missing or more than 7 days old. Change it with",
      "  `ptr recheck SECONDS` or `ptr recheck off`.",
      "* `ptr enemy add NAME`, `ptr ally add NAME`, `ptr enemy` to list. Allies always win.",
      "* `ptr hostile city mhaldor` makes everyone from Mhaldor count as an enemy",
      "  (`ptr hostile city mhaldor off` to undo). Houses work the same way.",
      "* `ptr list watch add NAME` makes your own lists.",
      "* `ptr set NAME class serpent` fixes a field by hand; lookups won't overwrite",
      "  it until `ptr unset NAME class`. `ptr note NAME text` attaches a note.",
      "* `ptr find class serpent`, `ptr find mhaldor`.",
      "* Type `honours NAME` as usual; PT reads the result.",
      "* `ptr ui` opens a small window of who is in your room, enemies first.",
      "",
      "The database is `pt_db.lua` in your Mudlet profile folder, shared by all",
      "characters on that profile. Settings are per character.",
      "",
      "## Where values come from",
      "",
      "Each field remembers its source. The order is: set by you (`ptr set`) >",
      "seen in play (`pt.observe`, class triggers) > HONOURS and the API. A lower",
      "source never replaces a higher one, so a class read from someone's attacks",
      "stays until a newer sighting changes it, and the API is only used when PT",
      "hasn't seen anything. The API's value is still kept, and `ptr NAME` shows",
      "\"API says jester\" when it disagrees. `ptr unset NAME class` drops back to",
      "the API value.",
      "",
      "Class triggers go in `src/08_class_signs.lua` (`pt.sign_list`): a regex for a",
      "line only that class makes, with the attacker's name as the first capture.",
      "Other packages can add them with `pt.class_sign(regex, class)`.",
      "",
      "## For other scripts (offense, curing, bashing)",
      "",
      "```lua",
      "pt.class(\"Bob\")         -- \"serpent\" or nil   (all values lower case)",
      "pt.city(\"Bob\")          -- \"mhaldor\", \"none\" (cityless) or nil",
      "pt.house(\"Bob\")",
      "pt.get(\"Bob\")           -- full record table, or nil",
      "pt.relation(\"Bob\")      -- \"enemy\" | \"ally\" | \"neutral\"",
      "pt.is_enemy(\"Bob\"), pt.is_ally(\"Bob\")",
      "pt.here()               -- names in your room",
      "pt.enemies_here(), pt.allies_here(), pt.is_here(\"Bob\")",
      "pt.is_online(\"Bob\")     -- from the last online check",
      "pt.observe(\"Bob\", \"class\", \"serpent\")  -- tell PT what you worked out in combat",
      "pt.source(\"Bob\", \"class\")  -- \"manual\" | \"seen\" | \"honours\" | \"api\", and when seen",
      "pt.class_sign([[^(\\w+) does a thing at you\\.$]], \"serpent\")  -- class trigger",
      "pt.api.lookup(\"Bob\", true, function(rec) ... end)",
      "```",
      "",
      "Events: `pt.arrived(name, relation)`, `pt.left(name, relation)`,",
      "`pt.room.changed`, `pt.person.updated(name, field, new, old)`,",
      "`pt.list.changed(list, name, added)`, `pt.checked(name, found)`,",
      "`pt.online.updated(count)`. If something raises `acs.target`, PT echoes what",
      "it knows about the new target.",
      "",
      "## Things to check in game",
      "",
      "Written from knowledge of Achaea, not tested on a live character yet:",
      "",
      "* HONOURS wording for city and house (`src/04_honours.lua`). If one isn't",
      "  picked up, paste the honours output and it can be matched exactly.",
      "* GMCP room messages were checked against your GMCP dump (Room.Players",
      "  includes you, RemovePlayer is a plain name).",
      "",
      "## Files",
      "",
      "| File | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `src/00_acs_core.lua` | shared ACS core (identical copy in every package) |",
      "| `src/00_core.lua` | pt namespace, settings, database file |",
      "| `src/01_people.lua` | records, lists, enemy/ally/hostile logic, read API |",
      "| `src/02_api.lua` | Achaea API lookups and online list |",
      "| `src/03_room.lua` | GMCP room tracking, arrivals, last seen |",
      "| `src/04_honours.lua` | HONOURS parsing |",
      "| `src/05_highlight.lua` | name colouring |",
      "| `src/06_commands.lua` | the `pt` commands |",
      "| `src/07_ui.lua` | room window |",
      "| `src/08_class_signs.lua` | class detection triggers (to fill in) |",
      "| `src/99_init.lua` | wiring |",
    },
  },
