    events = { "hb.beat", "hb.handler.off", "hb.paused", "hb.ready", "hb.removed", "hb.resumed" },
    guide = {
      "",
      "One timer beats every 250 ms and runs the handlers the other packages",
      "register with it: recomputing affliction and defence priorities, refreshing",
      "aliases, redrawing windows. Instead of each package running its own timers,",
      "they all hang off this one beat, which gives one place to pause, tune and",
      "profile everything.",
      "",
      "Built on the shared ACS core (`src/00_acs_core.lua`, an exact copy of",
      "`achaea-shared/acs_core.lua`), so it installs side by side with ss, ar, bs,",
      "pt, rm and in. Install order doesn't matter.",
      "",
      "## Install",
      "",
      "Mudlet: **Toolbox > Package Manager > Install**, pick `build/HB.mpackage`.",
      "You should see `[hb] loaded v0.1.0, beating every 250 ms`.",
      "",
      "Rebuild after editing `src/`: `python3 build.py`.",
      "Tests: `lua5.1 tests/test_hb.lua`, or `python3 tests/run_lua.py tests/test_hb.lua` (needs `pip install lupa`).",
      "",
      "## Commands",
      "",
      "| Command | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `hb status` | running or paused, interval, average and worst beat cost |",
      "| `hb list` | handlers in run order: priority, interval, watched keys |",
      "| `hb prof [reset]` | time spent in each handler, costliest first |",
      "| `hb interval [ms]` | show or set the beat (default 250, minimum 50) |",
      "| `hb pause` / `hb resume` | stop / restart the beat |",
      "| `hb once` | run one beat now |",
      "| `hb off NAME` / `hb on NAME` | switch a handler off or back on (remembered; `on` also revives one switched off after errors) |",
      "| `hb mark KEY` | flag a key as changed, for testing |",
      "| `hb budget [ms]` | beats slower than this are counted, and shown with `acs debug on` |",
      "",
      "Settings are saved per character in `<Mudlet home>/acs_<name>_hb.lua`.",
      "",
      "## For other packages",
      "",
      "HB is optional for the others: guard with `if hb then`. Register on load",
      "and again on `hb.ready`, which covers HB loading before or after you and HB",
      "being reinstalled. Registering the same name again replaces the handler, so",
      "this is reload safe:",
      "",
      "```lua",
      "local function hook()",
      "  hb.register(\"ss.priorities\", ss.recompute_priorities,",
      "    { owner = \"ss\", priority = 10, watch = { \"affs\", \"defs\", \"class\" } })",
      "  hb.register(\"ss.aliases\", ss.refresh_aliases, { owner = \"ss\", every = 1 })",
      "end",
      "if hb and hb.register then hook() end",
      "ss.on(\"hb.ready\", hook)",
      "```",
      "",
      "`hb.register(name, fn, opts)`; `fn(ctx)` gets",
      "`ctx = { beat, now, dt, changed }` (`dt`: seconds since this handler last",
      "ran; `changed`: the watched keys marked since then).",
      "",
      "| opts | meaning |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `priority` | lower runs first, default 50. Suggested bands: 0-19 state and priorities (ss), 20-39 offense (ar), 40-59 hunting (bs), 60-79 trackers (pt, rm, in), 80+ windows and display |",
      "| `every` | seconds between runs; default 0 = every beat |",
      "| `watch` | key or list of keys: run only when one was marked since the last run |",
      "| `urgent` | with `watch`: a mark runs a beat right away (next frame) instead of waiting up to 250 ms |",
      "| `owner` | package root, for `hb.unregister_owner(\"ss\")` |",
      "",
      "Other calls: `hb.unregister(name)`, `hb.mark(key)`, `hb.watch(event, key)`",
      "(mark a key whenever a Mudlet event fires), `hb.kick()` (one beat now,",
      "coalesced), `hb.pause()`, `hb.resume()`, `hb.set_interval(sec)`,",
      "`hb.get(name)`, `hb.beats`.",
      "",
      "Keys HB marks by itself from GMCP and the core: `affs`, `defs`, `vitals`,",
      "`room`, `players`, `items`, `class`, `char`. Packages can add their own",
      "(`hb.mark(\"ar.target\")`) and watch each other's.",
      "",
      "How it behaves:",
      "",
      "* A handler that throws is reported and skipped; the beat goes on. Five",
      "  errors in a row switch it off (`hb.handler.off` event) until `hb on NAME`.",
      "* A watched key marked between runs of a slow (`every`) handler is still",
      "  seen on its next run. A handler marking its own key runs once more, not",
      "  in a loop.",
      "* Reloading HB keeps every registered handler, its profile, and any",
      "  `hb.watch` wiring; the old timer is killed so only one beat runs.",
      "* Events raised: `hb.ready`, `hb.beat`(n) after each beat, `hb.paused`,",
      "  `hb.resumed`, `hb.handler.off`(name, error), `hb.removed` (HB uninstalled: the",
      "  beat stops and the `hb` global goes away).",
      "",
      "Things that must react to one prompt (sending a cure) should still run on",
      "the prompt or GMCP batch; use the beat for the recompute-and-tidy work, or",
      "mark the key `urgent`.",
    },
  },
