    guide = {
      "",
      "One place for everything that goes on Achaea's own queue (HELP QUEUEING,",
      "4.6.1): your aliases, AR's attacks, BS's flee, the `dg` alias. QM sends the",
      "QUEUE commands, keeps a copy of what's on the queue, and tells packages when",
      "the game runs something.",
      "",
      "Built on the shared ACS core (`src/00_acs_core.lua`, an exact copy of",
      "`achaea-shared/acs_core.lua`). It's in the Achaea bundle; on its own, install",
      "`build/QM.mpackage` (you should see `[qm] loaded v0.1.0`).",
      "",
      "Rebuild after editing `src/`: `python3 build.py`.",
      "Tests: `python3 tests/run_lua.py tests/test_qm.lua` (needs `pip install lupa`).",
      "",
      "## Typing it",
      "",
      "| Alias | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `qa [type] cmds` | QUEUE ADD: put it at the end |",
      "| `qc [type] cmds` | QUEUE ADDCLEAR: clear that queue type first |",
      "| `qp [type] cmds` | QUEUE PREPEND: put it at the front |",
      "| `qx` | CLEARQUEUE ALL |",
      "",
      "`type` is optional (default `eqbal`, change with `qm type`). It's taken as a",
      "type when it's a simple type name (`eq bal eqbal class ship para unbound",
      "stun free freestand full`), `eb`, or custom flags with a `!` in them",
      "(`eb!p!t`). So `qa put sword in pack` queues \"put sword in pack\" on eqbal;",
      "\"put\" is not read as flags.",
      "",
      "Several commands, split on your separator: `qc free stand|morph jaguar|might`.",
      "They go out as one game alias (`setalias qmyou stand/morph jaguar/might`,",
      "then `queue addclear free qmyou`), so all of them run on the same balance,",
      "like your old `ret` / `movement` aliases. SETALIAS is only re-sent when the",
      "commands change.",
      "",
      "| Command | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `qm list [game]` | what QM thinks is queued; `game` sends QUEUE LIST |",
      "| `qm clear [type]` | clear one type, or everything |",
      "| `qm add / addclear / prepend [type] cmds` | same as qa / qc / qp |",
      "| `qm type [t]` | default type for the short aliases |",
      "| `qm types` | the types and custom flags |",
      "| `qm sep [chars]` | what splits commands in qa / qc / qp (default `|`) |",
      "| `qm asep [chars]` | what goes between commands inside a game alias (default `/`, as SETALIAS wants) |",
      "| `qm gag on/off` | hide the `[System]` queue lines |",
      "| `qm alerts on/off` | send CONFIG SHOWQUEUEALERTS ON at login (on by default; QM needs those lines) |",
      "| `qm auto on/off` | the game's own auto queueing, CONFIG USEQUEUEING |",
      "| `qm forget` | reset QM's copy of the queue if it's gone wrong (sends nothing) |",
      "",
      "Settings are saved per character in `<Mudlet home>/acs_<name>_qm.lua`.",
      "",
      "## For other packages",
      "",
      "Guard with `if qm then`. AR's `ar.queue` and BS's flee already do.",
      "",
      "AR queues every attack as the game alias `qmar` (`alias = true`). The first",
      "attack puts `qmar` on the queue; if the plan changes before it runs (they",
      "cured something you want to reapply mid-balance), AR just sends",
      "`setalias qmar <new attack>` and the queue stays as it is. Once the game",
      "runs it, the next attack queues `qmar` again.",
      "",
      "```lua",
      "qm.queue(\"dstab bob curare kalmia\", { type = \"eqbal\", mode = \"addclear\", key = \"ar\" })",
      "qm.queue({ \"stand\", \"kick rat\" }, { type = \"free\", key = \"bash\",",
      "  on_run = function(e) bs.swung() end })      -- runs when the game runs it",
      "qm.addclear(\"touch shield\", \"free\")           -- add / addclear / addclearfull / prepend",
      "qm.clear(\"bal\")                               -- or qm.clear() for everything",
      "```",
      "",
      "| opts | meaning |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `type` | queue type or custom flags; default `qm.settings.type` |",
      "| `mode` | `add` (default), `addclear`, `addclearfull`, `prepend`, `insert`, `replace` |",
      "| `index` | for insert / replace |",
      "| `key` | who it's for; names the game alias for a group (`qm<key>`) and comes back on the entry. Use different keys for groups that should sit on the queue at the same time |",
      "| `together` | `false`: several commands go as separate queue entries, the first with `mode`, the rest `add` (what `ar.queue` did) |",
      "| `on_run` | `fn(entry)` when the game runs it |",
      "| `alias` | always go as the game alias `qm<key>`, even one command. If that alias is already waiting on the queue (queued in the last `reuse_for` seconds, default 10), only SETALIAS is sent and the queue is left alone |",
      "",
      "`qm.items` is the copy, oldest first: `{ type, cmd, cmds, key, at, on_run }`",
      "(`cmd` is the alias name for a group, `cmds` what's in it). It follows every",
      "QUEUE / CLEARQUEUE command that goes out, whether from `qm.queue`, another",
      "package's `acs.send`, or typed by you, and the game's lines. Seven entries at most (what",
      "the game allows now, though HELP QUEUEING still says ten); a game alias holds up",
      "to 20 commands, so a group takes one slot however long it is.",
      "",
      "Events: `qm.queued`(entry), `qm.ran`(entry), `qm.cleared`(type or \"all\"),",
      "`qm.full`(the entry the game refused).",
      "",
      "## Game lines it reads",
      "",
      "Checked in game:",
      "",
      "- `[System]: Running queued eb command: SMILE`: takes the entry off and runs `on_run` / `qm.ran`. The type is shown the way you queued it (`eb`, `free` ...)",
      "- `Cleared your queues.`: empties the copy",
      "- `[System]: Your queue is full.`: the newest command comes off the copy, you get a red line, and `qm.full`(entry) is raised",
      "- `[System]: Added SMILE to your eb queue.` and `[System]: Prepended ...`: only hidden with `qm gag on`",
      "",
      "The game's in-game alias separator is `/` (your client side one is `|`), so",
      "grouped commands are set as `setalias qm<key> a/b/c`.",
    },
  },
