    guide = {
      "",
      "Class-agnostic curing, defence keepup and offensive affliction tracking for",
      "Achaea, driven by GMCP.",
      "",
      "## Install",
      "",
      "In Mudlet: **Toolbox > Package Manager > Install**, pick `build/ACS.mpackage`.",
      "You should see `[acs] loaded v0.1.0`. Type `acs help`.",
      "",
      "To rebuild after editing `src/`: `python3 build.py`. To run the offline",
      "tests: `lua5.1 tests/test_acs.lua`.",
      "",
      "## First-time setup",
      "",
      "1. `acs status`: check that your class and vitals show up (GMCP is working).",
      "2. Choose a curing mode:",
      "   * `acs mode server` (default): Achaea's serverside curing does the curing.",
      "     ACS pushes your priorities and sip/moss thresholds to it (`acs sync`),",
      "     and adds what serverside can't do: class skill cures and keepup of",
      "     skill defences.",
      "   * `acs mode client`: ACS sends cures itself. It reads each affliction's",
      "     cure from GMCP (`Char.Afflictions.Add` includes it), falls back to its",
      "     own table, and uses tree and focus when the normal cure is blocked.",
      "3. For each class you play: raise all your defences by hand once, then",
      "   `acs keepup learn`. That class now has its own keepup list. Fix a command",
      "   with `acs defcmd <def> <command>` (append `@bal`, `@eq`, `@eqbal`, `@free`,",
      "   `@herb`, `@salve`, `@sip` or `@smoke` to say what it uses).",
      "4. Turn on class skill cures you have: `acs active list`, then e.g.",
      "   `acs active on fitness`. These are saved per class, too.",
      "5. Priorities: `acs prio <aff> <1-25>`. Make situational sets with",
      "   `acs profile copy <name>` and switch with `acs profile <name>`.",
      "",
      "Use `acs dry on` to watch what it would send without sending anything.",
      "",
      "## Offense (any class)",
      "",
      "* `t <name>` sets your target (and the in-game target via GMCP).",
      "* The target's afflictions are tracked; ACS removes them when it sees the",
      "  target eat, apply, smoke or focus, and notes when their tree is down.",
      "* `acs ta` shows the target's afflictions and lock state (soft/hard/true).",
      "* Scripts call `acs.enemy.give(\"asthma\")` or `acs.enemy.venom(\"kalmia\")`",
      "  when an attack lands. `acs.offense.next_aff(list)` and",
      "  `acs.offense.next_venoms(list, n)` pick what to give next.",
      "* `k` runs the attack module for your current class. See",
      "  `src/09_class_example.lua` for the pattern.",
      "",
      "## Files",
      "",
      "| File | What it does |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| `src/00_core.lua` | namespace, settings (saved per character), helpers |",
      "| `src/01_data.lua` | afflictions, cures, defences, class cures, venoms |",
      "| `src/02_state.lua` | GMCP vitals/afflictions/defences, balance tracking |",
      "| `src/03_engine.lua` | client-side cure engine, active class cures |",
      "| `src/04_keepup.lua` | per-class defence keepup |",
      "| `src/05_server.lua` | serverside curing sync |",
      "| `src/06_offense.lua` | target, queue, enemy tracker, lock detection |",
      "| `src/07_commands.lua` | the `acs` command set |",
      "| `src/08_ui.lua` | optional status window (`acs ui`) |",
      "| `src/09_class_example.lua` | example attack module |",
      "| `src/99_init.lua` | wiring: events, triggers, aliases |",
      "",
      "## Things to check in game",
      "",
      "These are written from knowledge of Achaea, not tested on a live",
      "character yet, so confirm them early:",
      "",
      "* Serverside command wording in `src/05_server.lua` (compare with `HELP CURING`).",
      "* Balance recovery lines in `src/99_init.lua`. If one doesn't match, the",
      "  balance still comes back after a timeout, just a bit slower.",
      "* Enemy cure messages in `src/06_offense.lua` (eat/apply/smoke/focus/tree).",
      "* Any affliction ACS calls \"unknown\": teach it with `acs cure <aff> <command>`.",
    },
  },
}
